			"url": "https://github.com/home-assistant/architecture/issues/483",
			"summary": "A maintainer proposes abandoning the in-progress OpenZWave 1.6 integration, which talks to a daemon over MQTT, in favour of the JavaScript Z-Wave JS driver behind a small socket server; he cites MQTT state bugs, daemon instability, a single C++ upstream developer going on break, and accepts discarding most of a year's work, listing pros and cons including migration difficulty.",
			"actorId": 6389780,
			"actorType": "human"
		},
		{
			"id": "architecture-483:comment:754965354",
			"kind": "comment",
			"actor": "balloob",
			"createdAt": "2021-01-05T23:34:03Z",
			"url": "https://github.com/home-assistant/architecture/issues/483#issuecomment-754965354",
			"summary": "The project lead agrees restarting is painful but necessary, and clarifies this adds a new integration while the two existing Z-Wave integrations stay.",
			"actorId": 1444314,
			"actorType": "human",
			"parentId": "architecture-483:issue:483"
